       The thread execution is suspended and does not consume any CPU time un‐
       til  the  condition  variable is signaled.  The _m_u_t_e_x must be locked by
       the calling thread on entrance to pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__wwaaiitt().  Before  return‐
       ing  to  the  calling thread, pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__wwaaiitt() re‐acquires _m_u_t_e_x (as
       per pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__lloocckk()).

       Unlocking the mutex and suspending on the condition  variable  is  done
       atomically.   Thus, if all threads always acquire the mutex before sig‐
       naling the condition, this guarantees that the condition cannot be sig‐
       naled (and thus ignored) between the time a thread locks the mutex  and
       the time it waits on the condition variable.  See CAVEATS below.

       pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__ttiimmeeddwwaaiitt() atomically unlocks _m_u_t_e_x and waits on _c_o_n_d, as
