CCAAVVEEAATTSS
       The implementation of the provided functions until glibc 2.25  used  an
       internal data lock.  This lock did not support priority‐inheritance and
       was  subject  to  unbounded  priority inversion, visible on a real‐time
       system.

       After the rewrite of the implementation in glibc 2.25 the usage of  in‐
       ternal  lock changed.  The internal lock is always acquired by the sig‐
       naling functions  pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__ssiiggnnaall()  and  pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__bbrrooaaddccaasstt().
       The  waiting  function acquires the lock if the waiting process was in‐
       terrupted.  The interruption can be caused for instance by a  specified
       timeout,  and  denoted  by the error value EETTIIMMEEDDOOUUTTAA, or by a received
       signal, which is denoted by the error value EEIINNTTRR.

